//! Excel's object model, described once (docs/architecture/OBJECT_MODEL.md).
//!
//! - [`descriptor`]: the interface facts of Excel's, Office's and the Add-in Designer's type
//!   libraries (IIDs, DISPIDs, vtable slots, exact parameter lists), generated by
//!   `tools/com-descriptor` from the installed type libraries and committed as JSON. No
//!   projection keeps its own member table.
//! - [`value`]: Automation values ([`AutoValue`]), the one value model every projection lowers to
//!   and from (VARIANT for COM, CalcVBA's Variant later, JavaScript values later).
//! - [`object`]: object identities ([`ObjectRef`]). A Range is a tracked
//!   [`calc_func::StoredReference`] from the session's reference tracker, never copied
//!   coordinates.
//! - [`model`]: the [`ObjectModel`] dispatch trait, the [`Handlers`] registry each profile fills,
//!   and the one refusal rule: a member the descriptor lists but no handler implements answers
//!   [`AutoError::NotModelled`], on every route.
//! - [`events`]: the [`EventSource`] a projection implements so the core can raise Excel's events.
//!
//! Member semantics live in profiles: application members that need no workbook in
//! `profile::values_only` (here, portable, shared by DNA OneCalc and DNA Calc); workbook members
//! in `calc_host::automation` (DNA Calc only); members that are COM by nature (COMAddIns,
//! CommandBars, ribbon) in `calc-com-host`. Projections translate; they never implement members.

pub mod descriptor;
pub mod events;
pub mod geometry;
pub mod model;
pub mod object;
pub mod profile;
pub mod value;

pub use descriptor::{Descriptor, Guid, InterfaceId, InvokeKind, Member, Param, ParamFlag, TypeInfo};
pub use events::EventSource;
pub use model::{AutoError, Call, Handler, Handlers, ObjectModel};
pub use object::{ObjectKey, ObjectRef};
pub use value::{AutoArray, AutoValue};
